Subject: [PATCH] ChFi3d: apply the periodic reconciliation at every corner, not
 only in the OnSame state

PerformOneCorner assembles two 2d points on the face at the end of the fillet
(pfac1, pfac2) and hands them to ChFi3d_ComputeCurves as Pardeb(3)/Parfin(3).
When that face is periodic and the corner vertex sits on the seam, the two
points come off the two different pcurve branches of the seam (u = 0 and
u = 2*pi). ChFi3d_Recale exists precisely to put them back on a common branch,
but here it is called only when the stripe is in the ChFiDS_OnSame state.

The sibling function IntersectMoreCorner performs the identical computation and
calls ChFi3d_Recale unconditionally (ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx:4031); the word
"onsame" does not appear in it at all.

ChFi3d_Recale is self-guarding: it does nothing unless the surface is U- or
V-periodic (ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx:447, 458), and even then only when the two
points are more than half a period apart (:451, :462). Dropping the guard is
therefore a no-op everywhere except the case it is meant to fix.

Measured on the owner's minimal pair (repro/cpp/seam_fillet_repro.cpp), fillet
radius 1.0, seam distance 0.000000 mm:

  before:  IsDone yes, Valid NO, volume 6224.4449, removed -374.9713, BOP DIRTY
  after:   IsDone yes, Valid yes, volume 5848.1055, removed +1.3681, BOP clean
           (analytic 1.3672)

The ten rows of the same sweep whose seam is far from the edge are unchanged,
byte for byte, at radii 0.25 / 0.5 / 0.55 / 1.0 / 2.0 / 3.0.

--- a/src/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
+++ b/src/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
@@ -804,7 +804,7 @@
     else {
       pfil2 = Fi2.PCurveOnSurf()->Value(Fi2.Parameter(!isfirst));
     }
-    if (onsame) ChFi3d_Recale(Bs,pfac1,pfac2,(IFadArc == 1));
+    ChFi3d_Recale(Bs,pfac1,pfac2,(IFadArc == 1));
 
     Pardeb(1)= pfil1.X(); Pardeb(2) = pfil1.Y();
     Pardeb(3)= pfac1.X(); Pardeb(4) = pfac1.Y();
